From c77b7d08c15577f93c0f56c5f3df943c6c6570c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <noreply@localhost>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 19:09:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] glm: mul1 prompt expert kernels (a mul1 checkpoint's 4-bit
 routed experts prefill on the prompt kernels)

The common EXL3 prompt kernels (tf_exl3_prompt_gu / _down / _down_b16, patch 0206's tf_exl3_prompt_gu_once and 0208's
tf_exl3_prompt_down_fuse) decoded mcg only, so a mul1 checkpoint (GLM-5.3-Derisked-EXL3-4bpw: 4-bit mul1 routed experts)
prefilled every routed expert through the grouped decode kernels (runSlots) and TF_GLM_PF_EXPERTS_ONCE /
TF_GLM_PF_DOWN_FUSE never applied.

Kernels: the prompt helpers take the codebook as a template parameter (dec2<CB>: mcg2 for mcg, exl3_decode.cuh's
decode2<CB> otherwise; decode_a8, decode_ag, tmain, tgateup, prompt_down_n, prompt_down_fuse, sums_n), defaulting to
mcg, and the module exports _mul1 copies of the 4-bit kernels: tf_exl3_prompt_gu_mul1, tf_exl3_prompt_down_mul1,
tf_exl3_prompt_down_b16_mul1, tf_exl3_prompt_down_fuse_mul1, tf_exl3_prompt_gu_once_mul1. In the e4m3 image
decode2<CB_MUL1> is mul1_e4m3 (patch 0214), so EXLR8 v0.7's experts take them too. The mcg kernels' SASS is unchanged
(cuobjdump -sass of tf_exl3_prompt_gu, _gu_once, _down_b16, _down_fuse: identical to the image before this patch).

Host: exl3_prompt.eligible admits mul1 layers whose gate/up and down are both 4-bit (3-bit and half-step mul1 keep the
grouped path); Kernels.run picks the _mul1 kernels by the layer's codebook.

Checks (spark6, GB10, sm_121):
  test-glm-exl3-host 24/24 (a 4-bit mul1 layer is eligible, a 3-bit one is not).
  exl3-prompt-k6: 4-bit mul1, one rotation and a rotation a pick, 1 / 64 / 1000 / 4096 rows: within 1e-3 RMS of
    runSlots (rms diff/rms <= 2.8e-4), 0.0813 of float64's tolerance (runSlots 0.0846). One layer, 4096 rows, top-8 of
    288, D 4096, N 1024 (GPU shared with another workload): mul1 prompt 33.5 ms median against runSlots 285 ms; mcg
    4-bit 33.0 ms.
  exl3-prompt-once / -e4m3: mul1 at 1 / 777 / 4096 rows and with clamp 7, xd and y byte-identical to rot_in + gu;
    control: mul1 and mcg give other bytes from the same words. (The mcg "fp32 SwiGLU (act_mode 1)" case fails
    before and after this patch with identical SASS; GLM runs act_mode 0.)
  glm-exl3-fuse / -e4m3 (TF_GLM_PF_DOWN_FUSE=1): 60/60 byte-equal, 15 of them 4-bit mul1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
